  "headline": "Ghana initiates discussions with Russia’s Rosatom for first nuclear power station",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Ghana has initiated discussions with Russia’s state nuclear energy corporation, Rosatom, regarding the establishment of the country’s first nuclear power station, President John Dramani Mahama disclosed. The announcement was made during his address at the Third Russia–Africa Summit in Moscow on October 29, 2026. President Mahama stated that Ghana is pursuing a diversified energy mix, including renewables, while advancing foundations for the peaceful use of nuclear energy to provide baseload capacity alongside existing hydropower and thermal sources. He noted that Russia possesses a comparative advantage in nuclear power and renewable energy that could yield results for Africa's industrialization. The President recalled that the Soviet Union provided Ghana with a two-megawatt nuclear reactor for research purposes in 1964 and that several Ghanaian nuclear scientists were trained in Russia to operate that reactor."
    }
  ]
}

