  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Addressing the Third Russia–Africa Summit in Moscow, Ghanaian President John Dramani Mahama commended Russian President Vladimir Putin for his willingness to resume trilateral talks regarding the conflict with Ukraine. Mahama expressed appreciation for Putin's call for a lasting peace agreement and security for both Russia and Ukraine, stating that global conflicts cause death, suffering, and disruptions to global logistics and value chains. While calling for conflicts to be resolved amicably, Mahama reaffirmed Ghana’s policy of non-alignment, noting that the country seeks partnerships that advance its development priorities."
